# License and IPR — Overview

**Document:** Secure Business Messaging Profile
**Version of this license overview:** 1.5
**Applies to:** the Secure Business Messaging Profile specification set (the umbrella profile v2.1 and later, the IETF Internet-Draft, the TS-shaped QERDS binding) and the companion artefacts in this repository.
**Date:** 2026-09-25
**Changed in 1.5:** this overview names the repository this snapshot is published from, in the attribution notice and in §7, and §2.1 and §3 list only the files the snapshot contains (checked by `make doc-lint`); the vision companion listed in 1.4 is not part of this snapshot.

---

## 1. What is licensed how

This repository uses a machine-readable, [REUSE](https://reuse.software)-compliant licensing scheme. Every file carries an `SPDX-License-Identifier` (inline or via `REUSE.toml`); the canonical license texts live in `LICENSES/`. In summary:

| What | License | Canonical text |
|------|---------|----------------|
| **Specification text and documentation** (the umbrella, the Internet-Draft, the TS-shaped binding, `docs/`, `README.md`, this file) | **CC BY 4.0** | [`LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt`](LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt) |
| **Reference code and machine-readable artefacts** (`scripts/`, `tests/`, `schemas/`, `samples/`, `edd-resolver-openapi.yaml`, build/CI files) | **MIT** | [`LICENSES/MIT.txt`](LICENSES/MIT.txt) |
| **Patent commitment** (Royalty-Free / RAND-Z) of contributors, for Conformant Implementations | RAND-Z | [`IPR.md`](IPR.md) |
| **Contribution terms** (inbound = outbound) | — | [`CONTRIBUTING.md`](CONTRIBUTING.md), [`IPR.md`](IPR.md) §5 |

Copyright and patent rights are independent legal mechanisms: a copyright license alone does not grant patent rights, and a patent commitment alone does not grant the right to reproduce or adapt the text. An implementer therefore needs **both** the copyright license (CC BY 4.0) **and** the patent commitment ([`IPR.md`](IPR.md)) to implement the Specification freely from the published text.

### 1.1 Ownership and independence

Copyright in the Specification and the companion artefacts is held by **Paolo De Rosa and the contributors** to this repository, in their personal capacity. This work is an **independent technical exploration**: it is not an official proposal, deliverable or position of the European Commission, of any Member State, or of any standards body, and the choice of copyright holder reflects exactly that independence. Should the work later be adopted by an institution or standards-developing organisation, the adopted deliverable would be governed by the adopting body's own copyright and IPR regime (see [`IPR.md`](IPR.md) §6 on the IETF and ETSI); this repository would remain available under the licenses described here.

